WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.852
This query uses CASE to handle several known date formats.

00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:08.977
Blank strings become NULL. ISO-style text can be cast to date.

00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:13.772
Slash-formatted text uses TO_DATE with a month-day-year pattern.

00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:17.107
Eight-digit text uses a year-month-day pattern.

00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:19.757
Anything else becomes NULL for review.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:23.262
The important idea is explicit, controlled parsing rather than guessing.

00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:27.732
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:30.802
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:30.802 --> 00:00:35.222
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:41.697
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:43.600
daylight-saving changes.
